# PACT — environment
#
# Every value here is OPTIONAL. `npm run dev` with no .env at all gives you a fully
# working app: the in-process store is seeded with the demo scenarios, and the Pact
# Builder falls back to a deterministic reader when no model is configured.
#
# Copy to .env.local (which is gitignored) and fill in only what you need.

# --- Sessions ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# HMAC key for the signed session cookie. Optional in development (one is generated per
# server start, so sessions reset on restart). REQUIRED in production, minimum 32 chars —
# the app refuses to start without it rather than silently minting cookies with a random
# per-instance secret that every other instance would reject.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# --- AI ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Enables the model-backed Pact Builder, Smart Review and Explain This Pact.
# Without it those features still work using lib/ai/fallback.ts, and the UI says so
# rather than implying a model wrote the output.
# Server-side only — this key is never sent to the browser.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Database ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT YET USED. The schema is complete in supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql, but the
# adapter that implements the Repository interface against it is not written yet, so
# setting these currently only logs a warning. See lib/db/index.ts.
#
# Until then PACT stores everything in-process: correct for local use and the demo,
# but it does not survive a server restart.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
